{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-bootstrap-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to check the\ncoverage setup under {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.setup.validation` and\nhelp establish or repair it with `habeas setup` before bootstrapping requirement\nevidence. It MUST direct agents to report conflicting configuration for review\nrather than overwrite project-specific nextest settings.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The requirement is about what the `habeas-bootstrap-requirements` skill directs agents to do. It prescribes no library, signature, type or delegation. Its obligations are to direct agents to (a) check the coverage setup, (b) help establish or repair it with `habeas setup` before bootstrapping evidence, and (c) report conflicting configuration rather than overwrite nextest settings. Those are content obligations, and the skill document is the only place they can be met. The supplied root, `assets/skills/habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md`, already carries an Implements edge to the requirement.\n\nI read the root's Workflow step 1 (`section[Bootstrap%20requirements]/section[Workflow]/paragraph@2cfd1398048b`). It says to check coverage readiness with `habeas status` before bootstrapping evidence. It notes that the validation test checks the saved `.config/nextest.toml` collector and default-profile rules. That matches `requirements.test-coverage.setup.validation`. It says to use `habeas setup` to establish or repair the integration. It says to report conflicting nextest settings for review and to preserve project-specific settings.\n\nThe skill therefore covers each clause, and no other implementation root is needed.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement sets three directives for the `habeas-bootstrap-requirements` skill. The reviewed test is `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bootstrap_checks_and_repairs_coverage_setup_and_preserves_conflicts]`. It loads the skill through `bundled_skill`, which joins SKILL.md and its references, and it asserts that the text contains each directive's wording.\n\n1. **Check the coverage setup under `requirements.test-coverage.setup.validation` before bootstrapping evidence.** The test asserts \"Before bootstrapping evidence, check coverage readiness with `habeas status`\". That covers both the check and its ordering. It also asserts \"saved `.config/nextest.toml` collector and default-profile rules\", which ties the check to what the validation requirement inspects.\n2. **Help establish or repair the setup with `habeas setup`.** The test asserts \"Use `habeas setup` to establish or repair\".\n3. **Report conflicting configuration for review rather than overwrite project-specific nextest settings.** The test asserts \"Report conflicting nextest settings for review\" and \"preserve project-specific settings\".\n\nI read workflow step 1 in `assets/skills/habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md`. It contains these sentences, so the assertions match the real skill text. Dropping any of the directives would fail the test.\n\nThe validation requirement's own checks (collector settings, selection rules, profile inheritance) belong to that requirement and its tests. They are not obligations of this skill requirement.",
